    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0816" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg802"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barlow, United
                        States marshal, to Mr. Hoar,
                        Attorney-General.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 2,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Attorney-General</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>There are not to exceed one hundred and seventy-five men. The balance escaped
                    ashore before capture. Who shall feed them? They will starve unless some one
                    does. Who must take charge of them, I or the admiral? Please answer. Unless
                    these men are discharged at once, I learn that a <hi rendition="#italic">habeas
                        corpus</hi> will be sued out for them. What return can be made to it?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FRANCIS C. BARLOW,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                            Marshal.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
